--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- multibody march: Rigid6 body, fixed and pinned rods, free points, chain, finite-EI cable
-- One standalone deck with every object type, in 70 m of still water, advanced together in the
-- default monolithic implicit step (bodyScheme monolithic).
-- Body 1 is a free Rigid6 buoy (150 t, 160 m^3) held by three taut nylon legs. Rod 1 is a
-- Body1 rod (a can fixed on the body, lumped into it); rod 2 is a Body1Pinned arm hanging from
-- the body, pinned at End A, with a nylon tether from its tip (R2B) to the seabed. A chain runs
-- from a body padeye through two Free points (a 100 kg float of 1 m^3 and a 400 kg clump) to an
-- anchor. A finite-EI power cable (EI = 1e4 N-m^2) hangs from another padeye to a seabed
-- termination; its pinned End A returns its end force to the body. bodyIC deck starts the body
-- from its deck pose, 3 m off its equilibrium in +X, so the run is a free-decay release: the body
-- swings back, the arm and the free points follow, and the cable top tension responds.
